---
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { t } from '../../lib/i18n';

const locale = 'en' as const;
const m = t(locale);
const promptPath = path.resolve(process.cwd(), '../task-paper-en.md');
const fullPrompt = fs.readFileSync(promptPath, 'utf8').trimEnd();
---

<BaseLayout locale={locale} title={m.aboutTitle}>
  <article class="prose-about max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="mb-2 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">{m.aboutTitle}</h1>
    <p class="text-[oklch(var(--foreground))]">
      I ran the same UI design task across dozens of agents and models and collected the results
      here. Cost difference between the most expensive and cheapest runs: 410×.
    </p>

    <h2>Goals</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>How usable and good the mockups are for real work</li>
      <li>How clean the internal structure is</li>
      <li>Cost of a solution</li>
      <li>How much the agent and reasoning level matter</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Procedure</h2>
    <p>
      One task: three screens for Recipe Scaler — desktop (1400px), mobile recipe (375px), promo
      (1400px). Tool: Paper MCP (and some Figma MCP). Mockup content in English. Fresh file per run;
      no manual fixes (except occasionally expanding a frame).
    </p>

    <h3>Constraints</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>No style or design-system guidance; clarifying questions skipped</li>
      <li>Max reasoning/effort except selected Opus 4.7 med runs</li>
      <li>No post-editing of designs — compare raw agent output</li>
      <li>English UI text — a mild cheat vs Cyrillic font support</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Prompt</h2>
    <p class="text-caption text-[oklch(var(--foreground))]">task-paper-en.md — full task text</p>
    <pre class="mt-2"><code>{fullPrompt}</code></pre>

    <h2>Quality tiers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Fancy</strong> — mostly Opus 4.7 family</li>
      <li><strong>Mid</strong> — clean-ish, still obviously AI</li>
      <li><strong>Slop</strong> — weak, especially promo</li>
      <li><strong>Failed tools</strong> — broken / empty layouts</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-caption text-[oklch(var(--foreground))]">
      Tiers are a draft from the post; edit <code>data/runs.json</code> to refine.
    </p>

    <h2>Conclusions</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5">
      <li>Opus leads. Expensive and clearly better than GPT 5.x on this task.</li>
      <li>Many non-lab models overfit benchmarks; real UI work exposes huge variance.</li>
      <li>A strong model makes “design by non-designers” less justified; designers still have work.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Links</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a class="underline" href="https://mikeozornin.ru/blog/all/llm-and-ui-design-en/">Post</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="underline" href="https://recipe-scaler.ru/#/about">recipe-scaler.ru</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
